    "text": "An electron of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>.0</mo><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>kg</mi></math> under the action of a magnetic field moves in a circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> at a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. If a proton of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.8</mo><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp;has to move in a circle of same radius and in the same magnetic field, then its speed must be",
